There shouldn't be anything explicitly debian specific in dgamelaunch.


> On Apr 25, 11:03 am, Ryan  Hampton <gro...@gmail.com> wrote:
>> Hello,
>>
>> I am having issues with dgamelaunch 1.4.7 on a gentoo machine.  I've
>> used strace which was suggested to others in here...not sure if I am
>> locating the errors properly.
>>
>> Here's the files it is not finding, for user 'test' with UID of 36:
>>
>> open("/var/games/nethack/save/36test.gz", O_RDONLY) = -1 ENOENT (No
>> such file or directory)

This would be dgamelaunch trying to back up the user savefile, and
this error is handled silently.


>> That is a brand new user that has never played a game.  The filename
>> is always 36username.gz.  Is this a red herring?  Is it just checking
>> if there is a previously saved game before starting a new one?
>>
>> Then I see this:
>>
>> access("/var/mail/test", F_OK)          = -1 ENOENT (No such file or
>> directory)
>>
>> Is it supposed to be creating directories for mail for each user?

No, /var/mail/test is a text file. dgamelaunch will try to remove the
file when a game starts, so the mail file doesn't contain old messages.
Again, this error is handled silently.


